            "review_title": "Review at Quan Vit CU CHI",
            "review_text": "Jeremy C\nPetaling Jaya, Malaysia2 contributions\n0\nGood Duck restaurant\nJun 2018 • Business\nThe restaurant is set under open, gazebo style dining areas (no air conditioning). Afternoon mealtimes can be warm but it is cool in the evening. The specialty are duck dishes but the roast duck is especially delicious. The offal and blood cake porridge, hot pot, steamed duck and some grilled dishes are decent. Comes with lots of salad on the side.\n\nPortions are relatively large, a Roasted duck (1/2 duck) is about 300,000D and enough for 3-4 if ordered with other dishes.\n\nModerate to high price for Vietnam standard. Expect to spend about 600,000D for 2 or 3 pax. Parking is available.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten June 20, 2018",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-03",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
