            "review_text": "vhp1967\nPoissy, France92 contributions\n0\nThe best lacquered duck I know\nFeb 2013 • Friends\nYou really have to know the place as it's not in downtown Saigon but it's definitely worth it - if you like duck. With part of my family Vietnamese, lacquered/roadted duck is something I'm familiar with but this was a treat. Duck is the specialty of the place and they serve you the lacquered breasts plus all the rest of the duck prepared as soup, etc. As for the place itself, it's a large wood-structure restaurant surrounded buy the vegetation so rather calm, especially for supper.\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten September 15, 2013",
